  "title": "Introduction to Rate Laws",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "2551649684",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "du45nzqoobl00e6",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "display": "block",
            "id": "1258292015",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/EE/EEC3A1E64C379208D2E3130FE82053D6/shutterstock_2408233867.jpg",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The concentrations of reactants usually influence the reaction rate, and a rate law or rate equation describes this relationship. Determining rate laws often involves the method of initial rates, where reaction rates are compared across multiple trials with varying initial reactant concentrations. From this analysis, we can identify the reaction orders and the value of the rate constant, and ultimately determine the rate law."
              }
            ],
            "id": "3355732035",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Rate laws link reaction rates to reactant concentrations and lead to integrated rate laws, which relate reactant concentrations to time. These integrated rate laws are useful for estimating the amount of reactant or product over time, such as determining the safe storage duration for radioactive materials."
              }
            ],
            "id": "6ocrbdijtyh52lu",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "e7nle5hoe5y52v3",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "editor": "slate",
        "id": "3857289316",
        "textDirection": "ltr",
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "i62u7i53ur53qky",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "ty8wrp9em4944bu",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "m4biuklvor5v370",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "recsnrvb347f3gv",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "As you have learned, the rate of a reaction is affected by the concentrations of reactants. A "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "rate law"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A mathematical equation showing the dependence of reaction rate on the rate constant and the concentration of one or more reactants. Also called "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "rate equation"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " or "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "differential rate law"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2499713871",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " or rate equation is a mathematical expression that describes the relationship between the rate of a chemical reaction and the concentrations of its reactants."
              }
            ],
            "id": "xwb6v7cvn1ir64l",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1792951319",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "fhn4carcvwtm6j2",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "x53b6tl2e8734ft",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "m7wwpj11gfdyysa",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "92z1fgiiakczleq",
            "items": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "In general, for the reaction:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " ",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                    "src": "\\mathrm{aA}\\;+\\;\\mathrm{bB}\\;+\\;\\mathrm{cC}\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm{products}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "the rate law takes this form:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " ",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                    "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;k\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack^m\\lbrack\\mathrm B\\rbrack^n\\lbrack\\mathrm C\\rbrack^p\\dots",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "[A], [B], and [C] represent the molar concentrations of reactants, and "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "k"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " is the "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "rate constant"
                          }
                        ],
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "A proportionality constant relating the rate of a chemical reaction at a given temperature to the concentration(s) of reactant(s). "
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "641980367",
                            "type": "p"
                          }
                        ],
                        "trigger": "hover",
                        "type": "popup"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", which is specific for a particular reaction at a particular temperature. The exponents "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "m"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "n"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", and "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "p"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " are usually positive integers (although it is possible for them to be fractions or negative numbers). The rate constant "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "k"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " and the exponents "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "m"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "n"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", and "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "p"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " must be determined experimentally by observing how the rate of a reaction changes as the concentrations of the reactants are changed. The rate constant "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "k"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " is independent of the concentrations of A, B, or C, but it does vary with temperature and surface area."
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "4062312215",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "dd"
              }
            ],
            "title": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Rate Law"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3281870615",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "type": "dl"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "7lo3iyol6yz8arl",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "40bx3l73occtmk4",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The exponents in a rate law describe the effects of the reactant concentrations on the reaction rate and define the reaction order. Consider a reaction for which the rate law is:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "v4krsvuqfb2dn9b",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "f74xd0tft1c47ch",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "vk4fe0jne0ycfqu",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;k\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack^m\\lbrack\\mathrm B\\rbrack^n",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "If the exponent "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " is 1, the reaction is first order with respect to A. If "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " is 2, the reaction is second order with respect to A. If "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " is 1, the reaction is first order in B. If "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " is 2, the reaction is second order in B. If "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " or "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " is zero, the reaction is zero order in A or B, respectively, and the rate of the reaction is not affected by the concentration of that reactant. The overall reaction order is the sum of the orders with respect to each reactant. If "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 0 and "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 0, the overall order of the reaction is 0 ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " + "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 0 + 0 = 0), referred to as a "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "zero-order reaction"
              },
              {
                "text": ". If "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 1 and "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 0, the overall order of the reaction is 1 ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " + "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 1 + 0 = 1), a "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "first-order reaction"
              },
              {
                "text": ". If "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 1 and "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 1, the overall order of the reaction is 2 ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "m"
              },
              {
                "text": " + "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 1 + 1 = 2), a "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "second-order reaction"
              },
              {
                "text": ".  "
              }
            ],
            "id": "2672938382",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "For the reaction:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "nvr2g2avtkqz1ym",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "flasiij0m0xpiii",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "g54jp218oeqm02j",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm H}_2{\\mathrm O}_2(aq)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;2\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm O}_2(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "the rate law:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "qcgis4dxm3qucns",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "z2sqoq0khtg43z0",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "iii4cddglzi3aho",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;k\\left[{\\mathrm H}_2{\\mathrm O}_2\\right]^1\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm{or}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm{Rate}\\; =\\;k\\left[{\\mathrm H}_2{\\mathrm O}_2\\right]",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "describes a reaction that is first order in hydrogen peroxide and first order overall (note that the superscript 1 is usually omitted). For the reaction:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "o6gkfsfi7d559uo",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "qssz6u77xygn8xq",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "8lvq29qkkl3e5lj",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "2\\;{\\mathrm C}_4{\\mathrm H}_6(g)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;{\\mathrm C}_8{\\mathrm H}_{12}(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "the rate law:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "bbbvsto00bmj1id",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "sztaxhm83jrps8z",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "otcohgqemnnjjwx",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;k\\lbrack{\\mathrm C}_4{\\mathrm H}_6\\rbrack^2",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "describes a reaction that is second order in C"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "4"
              },
              {
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "6"
              },
              {
                "text": " and second order overall. For the reaction:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1wam73nmvuot82t",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "5c5awiqcjq97rat",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "poafbw9bamj6sqt",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm I}_2(g)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{HI}(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "the rate law:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "spb47vv7rik30n3",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "ufyr2illmwiocbw",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "rxf65hcdir8eakv",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;k\\left[{\\mathrm H}_2\\right]\\left[{\\mathrm I}_2\\right]",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "describes a reaction that is first order in H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", first order in I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and second order overall."
              }
            ],
            "id": "8snicby1non9p8r",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "It is important to remember that rate laws are determined by experiment only and are not reliably predicted by reaction stoichiometry."
              }
            ],
            "id": "3hm3s571eahu9bz",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3789705152",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "An experiment shows that the reaction of nitrogen dioxide with carbon monoxide:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "d6f4ya1aghhg7ub",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "vtejhf3iqeglpvg",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "a9mwoj8c094q5qw",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\mathrm{NO}}_2(g)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{CO}(g)\\;\\;\\rightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm{NO}(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm{CO}}_2(g)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "is second order in NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and zero order in CO at 100 °C. What is the rate law for the reaction?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "6vbnn2mgxoznsry",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The rate law for the reaction will have the form:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "p0vsdjqp20vmop7",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ntd6aoq99l6hrr0",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "t3sb35gzkvtpr5d",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;k\\lbrack{\\mathrm{NO}}_2\\rbrack^m\\lbrack\\mathrm{CO}\\rbrack^n",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The reaction is second order in NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", so "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "m"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = 2. The reaction is zero order in CO, so "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "n"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = 0. The rate law is:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "hx5dmtyi62ndxo5",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "trnlugjgp5i4p34",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1myp41ms71gx8kw",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;k\\lbrack{\\mathrm{NO}}_2\\rbrack^2\\lbrack\\mathrm{CO}\\rbrack^0\\;=\\;k\\lbrack{\\mathrm{NO}}_2\\rbrack^2",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Remember that a number raised to the zero power is equal to 1, so [CO]"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "0"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = 1, and we can drop the concentration of CO from the rate equation: the rate of reaction depends solely on the concentration of NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". When we consider rate mechanisms later in this unit, we explain how a reactant’s concentration can have no effect on a reaction despite being involved in the reaction."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "qgtx3w4pyna9k7t",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1095935748",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  1,
                  0
                ]
              }
            },
            "type": "content"
          }
        ],
